WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.357 --> 00:00:12.218
Good day!

2
00:00:13.019 --> 00:00:19.523
My name is Melanie Hoff, and I'm a thirty-year-old zookeeper at the Auckland Zoo in New Zealand.

3
00:00:20.644 --> 00:00:27.729
I've been a zookeeper for seven years, but even now, in 2009, each day feels like a new

4
00:00:27.769 --> 00:00:32.232
beginning because you never know what to expect when animals are involved.

5
00:00:33.496 --> 00:00:36.737
Right now I am working with tigers and cheetahs.

6
00:00:37.877 --> 00:00:47.780
Last year something very extraordinary happened with our Sumatran tigers, Molek and Oz—they became the proud parents of

7
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.040
three tiger cubs.

8
00:00:50.301 --> 00:00:55.482
But before I get into that, let me tell you a bit more about how I became a

9
00:00:55.502 --> 00:00:59.583
zookeeper. As a little girl, I loved animals.

10
00:01:00.383 --> 00:01:02.284
I had a pet hamster and two dogs.

11
00:01:03.616 --> 00:01:10.080
My father was a veterinarian—an animal doctor—and every summer he would volunteer at the zoo.

12
00:01:11.341 --> 00:01:18.466
Sometimes I accompanied him, and I would spend my time following all the zookeepers around, asking lots of

13
00:01:18.546 --> 00:01:26.091
questions. I found out quickly that zoos aren't just parks where wild and exotic animals are on display.

14
00:01:27.512 --> 00:01:34.361
Zoos are places that create public awareness about the kinds of animals in our world, how they live,

15
00:01:34.881 --> 00:01:36.142
and how to protect them.

16
00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:44.669
In college I studied zoology, a branch of biology that deals with animals and animal life.

17
00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:53.557
I learned how to classify animals—from starfish to elephants— and by the time I graduated, I knew all

18
00:01:53.637 --> 00:01:58.681
about how different animals behave, what they like to eat, and where they live.

19
00:02:00.022 --> 00:02:06.621
Classroom study is very important, but zoos need people with hands-on experience with animals too.

20
00:02:07.521 --> 00:02:10.702
So I volunteered at the zoo, just like my dad.

21
00:02:11.983 --> 00:02:19.024
Right now I am taking care of our Sumatran tigers, which are the smallest of all tiger species.

22
00:02:19.865 --> 00:02:25.246
They are found in the wild only on the Indonesian island of Sumatra—nowhere else.

23
00:02:26.426 --> 00:02:32.268
Sumatran tigers are threatened because of the loss of their natural habitat and illegal poaching.

24
00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:38.364
Their habitat is being destroyed in part because the trees are being logged to make paper.

25
00:02:39.704 --> 00:02:45.869
And they are killed because tiger bones are used in traditional Chinese medicine, and hunters want their teeth

26
00:02:45.909 --> 00:02:47.150
and claws for trophies.

27
00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:54.975
It is part of my job to educate people about endangered species, but my first priority is to

28
00:02:55.055 --> 00:02:57.577
take care of the tigers to the best of my ability.

29
00:02:58.617 --> 00:03:00.779
My day starts around 7:30 a.m.

30
00:03:01.479 --> 00:03:06.646
Every morning the zookeepers from the different animal areas in the zoo have a brief meeting.

31
00:03:08.006 --> 00:03:14.469
We discuss any changes in the behavior, diet, skin quality, or coat condition of the animals in our

32
00:03:14.529 --> 00:03:22.372
care. Next my coworkers and I prepare food for the tigers, which is usually meat on the bone.

33
00:03:23.673 --> 00:03:29.855
We hide the food throughout the exhibit so our tigers can experience more natural foraging behavior.

34
00:03:31.156 --> 00:03:38.051
Then, from 8:15 until noon, we clean the animal enclosures and the exhibit areas.

35
00:03:39.412 --> 00:03:45.275
During cleaning the tigers are moved back and forth between the different areas or kept in cages in

36
00:03:45.295 --> 00:03:46.035
the tiger house.

37
00:03:47.236 --> 00:03:52.959
Most enclosures usually have ponds and climbing surfaces within a natural-looking environment.

38
00:03:53.919 --> 00:03:59.226
The water needs to be fresh, and all the areas where the animals spend time are secure and

39
00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:02.368
safe for both the animals and zoo personnel.

40
00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:11.234
New animals arrive at our zoo all the time; some are from other zoos, while others are rescued

41
00:04:11.274 --> 00:04:12.055
from the wild.

42
00:04:13.316 --> 00:04:18.819
If they are sharing an enclosure, they need to learn to get along with the other animals, so

43
00:04:18.919 --> 00:04:20.380
training is very important.

44
00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:29.635
For example, a zookeeper communicates with clear signals, which can be gestures or vocal cues, to tell animals

45
00:04:29.735 --> 00:04:33.377
to enter or exit certain sections of their enclosures.

46
00:04:35.479 --> 00:04:39.542
At our zoo we have two very friendly Asian elephants.

47
00:04:40.823 --> 00:04:48.308
Their keeper has trained these gigantic creatures to walk around the zoo and remain calm even when excited

48
00:04:48.428 --> 00:04:50.029
visitors scream with delight.

49
00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:58.859
We also have daily animal encounters: specified times when visitors can see and learn about some of their

50
00:04:59.019 --> 00:05:05.883
favorite animals—such as giraffes, orangutans, and even snakes—up close.

51
00:05:07.144 --> 00:05:12.427
The keepers explain the animals' habits, what they like to eat, and how they like to play.

52
00:05:13.327 --> 00:05:19.831
Sometimes the zookeepers will allow visitors to pet some of the animals, but safety is always a top

53
00:05:19.851 --> 00:05:24.838
priority. It's important to remember that the zoo is not a circus.

54
00:05:25.898 --> 00:05:31.982
In the past zoo animals were kept in small cages and made to do tricks to entertain people.

55
00:05:33.002 --> 00:05:35.223
Thankfully things have changed.

56
00:05:36.664 --> 00:05:41.607
As you can see, being a zookeeper is a lot of work, but it's also a lot of

57
00:05:41.727 --> 00:05:48.611
fun. One time a television crew was filming at our zoo, and the soundman held up a big

58
00:05:48.691 --> 00:05:50.752
microphone with a fluffy cover on it.

59
00:05:51.952 --> 00:05:55.575
One of our cheetahs noticed this fluffy thing and decided to play with it.

60
00:05:56.156 --> 00:05:57.857
People burst out laughing.

61
00:05:58.898 --> 00:06:00.559
But scary things happen too.

62
00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:07.084
One day I surprised a gorilla when I touched her, and she turned around and almost bit my

63
00:06:07.124 --> 00:06:13.850
hand. It was entirely my fault, and I was reminded again that these are wild animals.

64
00:06:15.171 --> 00:06:18.093
The saddest part of my job is when an animal dies.

65
00:06:19.394 --> 00:06:25.179
I still remember when Nisha, one of our Sumatran tigers, died in May 2006.

66
00:06:25.799 --> 00:06:27.601
All of us at the zoo still miss her.

67
00:06:28.561 --> 00:06:34.666
But the best part of my job is when we welcome new animal babies into our zoo family.

68
00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:44.733
In early 2008 Nisha's younger sister Molek mated with Oz, another Sumatran tiger, and gave birth in June

69
00:06:44.813 --> 00:06:48.156
to three cubs―two males and one female.

70
00:06:48.928 --> 00:06:51.870
The entire country was ecstatic over the news!

71
00:06:53.191 --> 00:06:57.293
Being a zookeeper doesn't pay very well, and it involves long hours.

72
00:06:58.714 --> 00:07:01.236
So why do so many people want to become zookeepers?

73
00:07:02.536 --> 00:07:08.580
Because we love animals and want to draw attention to the fragile planet we all live on together.

74
00:07:09.681 --> 00:07:17.661
For example, fewer than four hundred Sumatran tigers remain in the wild, so the publicity surrounding the birth

75
00:07:17.701 --> 00:07:22.382
of these cubs educated people about how endangered Sumatran tigers are.

76
00:07:23.442 --> 00:07:27.883
Suddenly everyone wanted to help save Sumatran tigers from extinction.

77
00:07:29.004 --> 00:07:35.486
Through education the public comes to understand the need to preserve any species that is in danger of

78
00:07:35.546 --> 00:07:37.846
being destroyed and lost forever.

79
00:07:39.527 --> 00:07:43.508
I believe there is nothing more rewarding than my work as a zookeeper.

80
00:07:44.681 --> 00:07:48.858
It is the best job a human can do for the earth and all its living things.
